  "final_message": "If you don't pass `max_attempts`, `retry.call_with_retry()` makes up to 4 attempts (the first try plus 3 retries) before it raises the last exception.\n\n- **Where the 4 comes from:** In `retry.py`, `max_attempts` defaults to `None`. When it's `None`, the function uses `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`, and the loop `for _ in range(attempts)` calls `fn()` at most 4 times.\n- **Numbers to ignore:** `RETRY_LIMIT = 5` in `decoy_backoff.py` and `MAX_RETRIES = 3` in `decoy_network.py` are never imported by `retry.py`, so they don't change the answer.\n- **Other files:** `main7.py` calls it without `max_attempts`, so it gets the default. `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` only has an empty bundle list and has nothing to do with retries.\n\nANSWER: 4",
